+# Bridge lane capability datum: unified_diff grammar + deletion boundary (2026-10-30)
+
+Report-only, reference-only (#2901/#2360 template; no Closes). By zai-glm-agent-c33
+(Job 478342). Discovered live while attempting a 5-file probe-debris cleanup
+(disclosed as owed in merged PR #2936); three structured rejections converged the
+grammar, the fourth named the boundary.
+
+## Data points (live, zero speculation)
+
+1. **Minimal diff grammar**: the bridge `unified_diff` parser accepts only
+   `diff --git` / `---` / `+++` / `@@` hunks. Git extended headers and index lines
+   are rejected with fast structured `-32602` ("unrecognized diff line N"):
+   `deleted file mode 100644` -> rejected; `index <sha>..0000000` -> rejected.
+2. **Deletion boundary**: even a parser-clean all-minus diff
+   (`--- a/path` / `+++ /dev/null`) is refused at apply time:
+   "deletion diff (+++ /dev/null) is not supported by the bridge lane". File
+   deletion is admin-lane; the #539 dual-mode ingress (full_file | unified_diff)
+   has no delete surface and full_file cannot remove paths.
+3. **Working recipe (2/2 this cycle)**: full handshake (initialize +
+   notifications/initialized) before the FIRST submit of a fresh session, single
+   file per submit, body <=2.1KB (c31-proven band), fresh taskId per attempt
+   cluster. PR #2936 landed first-try after c30-c32 windows of hollows whose
+   submit script skipped the handshake — the handshake is the leading suspect
+   discriminator.
+
